
config PWM_INGENIC
        tristate "Ingenic PWM support"
        depends on SOC_X2500
        help
          Generic PWM framework driver for Ingenic soc based
          machines.

          To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
          will be called pwm-ingenic.

config PWM_INGENIC_V2
        tristate "Ingenic PWM V2 support"
        depends on SOC_X2000_V12 || SOC_X2000 || SOC_M300 || SOC_X2100
        help
          Generic PWM framework driver for Ingenic soc based
          machines.
          Support SOCs: X2000,

          To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
          will be called pwm-ingenic.


config PWM_INGENIC_V2_GET_STATE
        bool "Ingenic PWM V2 .get_state hardware readback support"
        depends on PWM_INGENIC_V2
        default n
        help
          NebulaOS PWM state readback patch (2026-08-xx): implements the
          missing .get_state callback for pwm-ingenic-v2.c, which
          previously only implemented .apply. Without .get_state, the
          generic PWM core's one-shot readback at PWM request time
          (drivers/pwm/core.c:pwm_device_request()) leaves a consumer's
          cached state at a synthetic all-zero/disabled value regardless
          of what the hardware is actually doing.

          COMMON_MODE channels (the default - see mode_sel[] in
          pwm-ingenic-v2.c) get an exact enabled/period/duty_cycle/
          polarity readback, agreeing with the .apply path to within one
          hardware tick. DMA_MODE channels (only reachable via a debug
          sysfs store handler, not expected on a real backlight channel)
          have no simple duty/period register - period/duty_cycle are
          reported as 0 and explicitly NOT claimed exact; see the new
          get_state_exact sysfs attribute and the exported
          ingenic_pwm_channel_get_state_is_exact().

          See docs/NEBULAOS_PWM_STATE_READBACK_REPORT.md for the full
          PRESCALE-ambiguity trace and round-trip test results.

          Disabled by default - this project's convention is to never
          silently change an already-shipping driver's behavior until
          live-hardware-qualified. If unsure, say N.

config PWM_INGENIC_V3
        bool "Ingenic V3 PWM support"
        depends on SOC_X1600 || SOC_X2600 || SOC_AD100
        help
          Generic PWM framework driver for ingenic PWM-V3
          machines.

config JZ_PWM_GPIO_TRIGGER
        bool "pwm gpio trigger support"
        depends on PWM_INGENIC_V3
        default n

config PWM_DUMP
    bool "Enable PWM dump feature"
    default y
    help
        Enable this option to generate sysfs attributes for PWM dump.
